        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0752" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg632"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Morgan to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Seoul,
                                Korea</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-12-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 6, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 41.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With the confirmation below of my telegram
                    of the 28th of November in reference to my departure from Seoul, I have the
                    honor to inclose copies of the notes addressed by me on that day to the Korean
                    minister for foreign affairs, to our consul-general for Korea, and to the chargé
                    d’affaires of the American legation at Tokyo, informing them that in conformity
                    with your instructions I had intrusted the archives and property of the legation
                    to the care of the American consul-general at Seoul and was about to withdraw
                    from Korea. * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin V. Morgan.</hi></signed></closer>




